{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/pulls/680","id":4233999261,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAWoOrs78XbOd","html_url":"https://github.com/theskumar/python-dotenv/pull/680","diff_url":"https://github.com/theskumar/python-dotenv/pull/680.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/theskumar/python-dotenv/pull/680.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/issues/680","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/pulls/680/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/pulls/680/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/issues/680/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/statuses/439f4fe44d632a7a207ed6813053317c44a3a263","number":680,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix: make values containing backslashes round-trip through set_key","user":{"login":"dchaudhari7177","id":111210939,"node_id":"U_kgDOBqDxuw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111210939?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177","html_url":"https://github.com/dchaudhari7177","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #661.\n\n## Problem\n\n`set_key` writes single-quoted values and escapes single quotes, but not backslashes. The single-quoted-value parser decodes `\\` and `\\'`, so a value containing a backslash does not survive a write/read round-trip:\n\n```python\n>>> dotenv.set_key(\".env\", \"PATH\", r\"C:\\Users\")   # file gets PATH='C:\\Users'\n>>> dotenv.get_key(\".env\", \"PATH\")\n'C:Users'\n>>> dotenv.set_key(\".env\", \"RE\", r\"\\d+\")\n>>> dotenv.get_key(\".env\", \"RE\")\n'd+'\n```\n\nWindows paths and regular expressions are the common victims.\n\n## Fix, part 1 — escape on write\n\n`value_to_set.replace(\"\\\\\", \"\\\\\\\\\").replace(\"'\", \"\\'\")`. Backslashes first, so the backslash introduced by the quote escaping is not escaped again.\n\n## Fix, part 2 — the write side alone is not enough\n\nWith only part 1, a value ending in a backslash is still broken, and breaks its neighbours too:\n\n```\nA='back\\'\nB='sentinel'\n```\n\n`_single_quoted_value` was `'((?:\\'|[^'])*)'` — it knows `\\'` is an escape but not `\\`. So in `back\\'` the second backslash pairs with the closing quote as `\\'`, the match keeps going, and since `[^']` also matches newlines it runs into the next line. The binding then fails `_end_of_line`, error recovery kicks in, and `B` is lost as well.\n\nBoth quoted-value patterns now say \"a backslash escapes the next character\":\n\n```python\n_single_quoted_value = make_regex(r\"'((?:\\.|[^'\\])*)'\", extra_flags=re.DOTALL)\n_double_quoted_value = make_regex(r'\"((?:\\.|[^\"\\])*)\"', extra_flags=re.DOTALL)\n```\n\n`re.DOTALL` keeps multi-line quoted values working, which the old `[^']` allowed.\n\nThis is not a behaviour change for anything that parsed correctly before — the captured group is identical for every input the old pattern handled, and `decode_escapes` is untouched. It only changes inputs that previously failed to parse. Hand-written `A='C:\\Users\\name'` still yields `C:\\Users\\name`, and `A='b\\'c'` still yields `b'c`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_set_key` gains three cases pinning the written form for `b\\c`, `b\\` and `b\\'c`.\n- New `test_set_key_round_trips` parametrizes ten values (Windows paths with and without a trailing separator, regexes, quotes, empty) and asserts both that the value comes back intact and that a following key is still readable — that second assertion is what catches the line-swallowing.\n- `test_parse_stream` gains five cases for escaped backslashes in both quote styles, including the two-binding case.\n\n`pytest tests/` passes. The two `test_cli.py::test_run_*` failures on my machine are pre-existing and Windows-specific (they reproduce on an unmodified checkout).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[{"id":11851224623,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAWoOrs8AAAACwmNWLw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/labels/inprogress","name":"inprogress","description":"Being actively reviewed/worked on","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08T09:09:30Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T15:23:35Z","closed_at":"2026-08-16T15:23:35Z","merged_at":"2026-08-16T15:23:35Z","merge_commit_sha":"f7b18d9c72d1abcc2ad4023424b84f5bee30d266","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"dchaudhari7177:fix/set-key-escape-backslash","ref":"fix/set-key-escape-backslash","repo":{"id":1327583352,"node_id":"R_kgDOTyFQeA","name":"python-dotenv","full_name":"dchaudhari7177/python-dotenv","owner":{"login":"dchaudhari7177","id":111210939,"node_id":"U_kgDOBqDxuw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111210939?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177","html_url":"https://github.com/dchaudhari7177","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari7177/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dchaudhari717